ry section.\\\"}},{\\\"candidates\\\":[{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"15\\\",\\\"created_turn\\\":3,\\\"goal_id\\\":3,\\\"id\\\":7,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"candidate\\\",\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"The craft store makes a third of its sales in the fabric section and a quarter of its sales in the jewelry section. Therefore, the fraction of sales in the fabric section is 1/3 and the fraction of sales in the jewelry section is 1/4. The total fraction of sales in the fabric and jewelry sections is 1/3 + 1/4 = 7/12. The remaining fraction of sales, which is in the stationery section, is 1 - 7/12 = 5/12. Given that the total sales are 36, the number of sales in the stationery section is 36 * (5/12) = 15.\\\",\\\"revises\\\":null}],\\\"goal\\\":{\\\"candidates\\\":[7],\\\"child_goals\\\":[],\\\"created_turn\\\":0,\\\"id\\\":3,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"goal\\\",\\\"parent_goal\\\":0,\\\"task\\\":\\\"Determine the fraction of sales in the stationery section.\\\"}},{\\\"candidates\\\":[{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"21\\\",\\\"created_turn\\\":4,\\\"goal_id\\\":4,\\\"id\\\":8,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"candidate\\\",\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"The craft store made a third of its sales in the fabric section, which is 36 / 3 = 12 sales. A quarter of its sales were in the jewelry section, which is 36 / 4 = 9 sales. The rest of the sales were in the stationery section. Therefore, the number of sales in the stationery section is 36 - 12 - 9 = 21.\\\",\\\"revises\\\":null}],\\\"goal\\\":{\\\"candidates\\\":[8],\\\"child_goals\\\":[],\\\"created_turn\\\":0,\\\"id\\\":4,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"goal\\\",\\\"parent_goal\\\":0,\\\"task\\\":\\\"Calculate the number of sales in the stationery section.\\\"}}],\\\"previous_exact_attempts\\\":[],\\\"remaining_turns\\\":7,\\\"root_problem\\\":\\\"A craft store makes a third of its sales in the fabric section, a quarter of its sales in the jewelry section, and the rest in the stationery section. They made 36 sales today. How many sales were in the stationery section?\\\",\\\"schema_version\\\":\\\"workspace-hy